Text data extraction is the automated process of identifying and pulling specific pieces of information from unstructured text documents. This could involve extracting names, dates, addresses, product codes, or any other relevant data points from sources like invoices, contracts, emails, reports, or web pages. It's a fundamental step in making sense of large volumes of text data, transforming it into structured information that can be easily analyzed, stored, or used in other applications.
Several techniques are employed for text data extraction. Rule-based systems use predefined patterns and rules (often regular expressions) to locate and extract specific information. Machine learning methods, particularly Natural Language Processing (NLP), offer more flexibility. 
